Data Ingestion
Method
Data was loaded using Snowsight's Load Data wizard, which internally uses Snowflake's COPY INTO command with an auto-managed stage.

File Format
CREATE OR REPLACE FILE FORMAT CSV_FORMAT
    TYPE = CSV
    SKIP_HEADER = 1
    FIELD_OPTIONALLY_ENCLOSED_BY = '"'
    NULL_IF = ('', 'NULL', 'null')
    EMPTY_FIELD_AS_NULL = TRUE;
Load Validation
After loading, row counts were verified against expected values to confirm complete ingestion:

SELECT 'RAW_CUSTOMERS' AS table_name, COUNT(*) AS row_count FROM RAW_CUSTOMERS
UNION ALL SELECT 'RAW_ORDERS', COUNT(*) FROM RAW_ORDERS
-- ... (all 9 tables verified)
Data Protection
RAW tables use CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS to prevent accidental data loss when re-running the setup script. This protects loaded data from being overwritten.

Data Transformations
STAGING Layer
The STAGING layer applies the following transformations:

Transformation	Example
City name standardization	INITCAP(TRIM(customer_city))
State code normalization	UPPER(TRIM(customer_state))
Status standardization	LOWER(TRIM(order_status))
Delivery days calculation	DATEDIFF('day', purchase, delivery)
Total item value	price + freight_value
Product volume	length * height * width
English category names	JOIN with translation table
Review response time	DATEDIFF('day', creation, answer)
NULL filtering	WHERE order_id IS NOT NULL
